#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:4
#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:12
msgid "Values"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:14
msgid ""
"Kalanjiyam's mission is to make the classical Knowledge Systems tradition"
" radically accessible, powered by BharatGen. This mission is guided by "
"several core values that shape everything we do."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:19
msgid "Classical Knowledge as human heritage"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:21
msgid ""
"Ancient Knowledge Systems literature is part of our collective human "
"heritage, and we want to preserve and share this knowledge for future "
"generations. This vast heritage encompasses not just medicine and "
"alchemy, but also philosophy, spirituality, and practical wisdom that has"
" been passed down through centuries."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:28
msgid ""
"We believe that this knowledge belongs to all of humanity and should be "
"freely accessible to anyone who wishes to learn from it, regardless of "
"their background, location, or economic status."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:34
msgid "Radical accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:36
msgid ""
"We believe that knowledge should be accessible to everyone. This means "
"not just making texts available online, but also providing tools and "
"resources that make the content understandable and useful to people at "
"all levels of expertise."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:42
msgid ""
"Our platform includes features like word-by-word analysis, integrated "
"dictionaries, and contextual explanations to help readers understand "
"complex ancient texts. We also provide translations and commentaries to "
"make the content accessible to all readers."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:48
msgid "Open collaboration"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:50
msgid ""
"We believe that the best way to preserve and improve our knowledge base "
"is through open collaboration. Our platform allows users to contribute "
"corrections, translations, and additional content, creating a community-"
"driven resource that grows and improves over time."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:57
msgid ""
"We welcome contributions from scholars, students, and enthusiasts from "
"around the world, recognizing that diverse perspectives and expertise "
"enrich our understanding of these heritage traditions."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:63
msgid "Cultural respect"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:65
msgid ""
"We approach these ancient traditions with deep respect for their cultural"
" and historical significance. We work closely with scholars and "
"practitioners to ensure that our representations are accurate and "
"respectful of the tradition's integrity."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:71
msgid ""
"We also recognize that this heritage is a living tradition that continues"
" to evolve and adapt. Our goal is to preserve the historical texts while "
"also supporting contemporary practice and scholarship."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:77
msgid "Technical excellence"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:79
msgid ""
"We believe that the best way to serve our mission is through technical "
"excellence. Powered by BharatGen, our platform is built with modern AI "
"and web technologies that provide a fast, reliable, and user-friendly "
"experience."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/values.html:85
msgid ""
"We continuously improve our tools and infrastructure to better serve our "
"users and preserve the texts in our care. We also make our code open "
"source so that others can learn from and build upon our work."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/base.html:16
#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/base.html:21
#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:16
#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/proofing.html:16
msgid "People"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/base.html:27
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Kalanjiyam receives contributions from dozens of volunteer <a "
"href=\"%(proofers_url)s\">proofers</a>, <a "
"href=\"%(translators_url)s\">translators</a>, and <a "
"href=\"%(coders_url)s\">programmers</a> who are passionate about making "
"Sanskrit accessible to all."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:23
msgid "Our core team builds and maintains the overall project."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:31
msgid "Arun Prasad"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:31
msgid "Founder and Project Lead"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:34
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Arun is the creator of <a href=\"%(lso)s\">learnsanskrit.org</a> and the "
"Sanskrit short story project <a href=\"%(amarahasa)s\">Amarahasa</a>. "
"Broadly, his work explores how software and digital tools can make "
"Sanskrit literature radically accessible. Arun has an MS in Computer "
"Science and a minor in Classics with a focus on Homeric Greek, both from "
"Stanford University. By profession, he is a former Google Research "
"engineer that works in climate fintech."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:46
msgid "Ashwin Ramaswami"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:46
#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:59
msgid "Core Engineering"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:47
msgid ""
"Ashwin has worked on a variety of projects around open source software "
"development, digital humanities, cloud infrastructure and architecture, "
"and cybersecurity. His interests in Sanskrit include Vedic texts and "
"Vedantic commentaries. Ashwin holds a B.S. in Computer Science from "
"Stanford University and is currently pursuing a J.D. degree at Georgetown"
" University Law Center, where he works on technology law and policy."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:59
msgid "Kishore Chitrapu"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:60
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Kishore contributes to <a href=\"%(sf)s\">Saraswati Films</a> and related"
" projects. He is interested in learning methods and building free tools "
"for sādhanā and sustainable living. He enjoys learning from Vedic wisdom."
" Professionally, he works as a Director of Engineering and is currently "
"building finance data platforms. Finally, Kishore enjoys any time with "
"his family and friends and is grateful for their support."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:74
msgid "Suhas Mahesh"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:74
msgid "Text Curation and Sourcing"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/core.html:75
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Suhas Mahesh is a <a href=\"%(schmidt)s\">Schmidt Science Fellow</a> at "
"the University of Toronto, where his research explores building bespoke "
"materials for a low-carbon future. Suhas has a PhD in physics from the "
"University of Oxford, where he was a <a href=\"%(rhodes)s\">Rhodes "
"scholar</a>. Suhas is a expert on Sanskrit and Prakrit literature, and "
"his current projects include an anthology of Sanskrit and Prakrit love "
"poetry in translation (HarperCollins 2023), and a translation of the "
"<cite>Nilakantha-vijaya-champu</cite>, an ornate retelling of the myth of"
" the churning of the ocean (Murty Classical Library of India)."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/about/people/proofing.html:23
msgid ""
"Dozens of proofers have contributed to Kalanjiyam. Here we recognize our "
"most active contributors."
msgstr ""

