#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:81
msgid ""
"Proofing, short for \"proofreading,\" is when people like you create "
"high-quality Sanskrit text that everyone can use and enjoy. All of our "
"proofing projects are based on scans of physical books."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:97
msgid "Gray pages have not been proofed."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:98
msgid ""
"Starting on a gray page is a great way to help out, because you will be "
"the first person to read and transcribe it."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:105
msgid "Yellow pages have been proofed once."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:106
msgid ""
"Working on a yellow page means reviewing someone else's work to catch any"
" mistakes they might have missed."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:113
msgid "Green pages have been proofed twice."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:114
msgid "These pages are considered finished and do not need any more proofing."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:122
msgid ""
"To proof a page, simply click on its page number in the project view. "
"This opens our side-by-side page editor:"
msgstr ""

