msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:125
msgid "Shows the scan of the original printed book page."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:126
msgid "Text on the left:"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:126
msgid "Contains the machine-transcribed (OCR) text that you will edit."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:129
msgid ""
"Compare the text on the left with the image on the right. Correct any "
"typos, missing characters, or formatting errors so the text matches the "
"original scan."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:135
msgid "Project Creation & Preparation Checks"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:136
msgid ""
"1. Scope: We preserve and transcribe manuscripts and books related to "
"traditional literature, philosophy, grammar, dictionaries, and medicine."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:137
msgid ""
"2. Avoid Duplication: Check our library and public repositories first to "
"verify whether this work has already been digitized."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:138
msgid ""
"3. Scan Quality: Upload clear, high-resolution scans (.pdf, .docx, or "
"multi-page .jpg/.png) to ensure optimal OCR and proofreading accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:141
msgid "When proofing, follow these simple guidelines:"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:144
msgid "Match the original text."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:144
msgid ""
"Transcribe the text as it appears in the book scan, even if you notice "
"spelling errors in the original source."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:145
msgid "Use standard Sanskrit transliteration."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:145
msgid ""
"Enter text in Devanagari or standard Roman IAST as requested by the "
"project guidelines."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:146
msgid "Preserve verse structures."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:146
msgid "Keep danda (।) and double danda (॥) marks in their original locations."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:154
msgid "What if I am not sure about a character?"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:155
msgid ""
"If a character is blurry or smudged in the scan, do your best guess or "
"use the [?] markup button in the editor toolbar to flag it for the next "
"reviewer."
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:159
msgid "Can I upload my own book scan?"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:160
msgid ""
"Yes! Registered users can upload PDF scans or archive.org identifiers "
"using the"
msgstr ""

#: kalanjiyam/templates/proofing/beginners-guide.html:160
msgid "button."
msgstr ""

